    {
      "week": 5,
      "day": 30,
      "title": "León - Rest day",
  "distance": "0,0 km",
  "time": "Rest",
  "short_desc": "Back pain, Podcast recording, and Pasta on the Plaza Regla in León",
  "long_desc": " The day started a bit differently, Roy needed to have his back checked, so we went to a clinic in León to book an appointment. Luckily, we got a time slot for 10:00 a.m. the next morning, which felt both quick and reassuring. The rest of the morning was spent doing a bit of shopping to refresh our travel wardrobe, after 30 days on the road, a few items definitely needed replacing. At this point, you feel the wear not only on your body but on your clothes and gear too. In the afternoon, we had a meeting with sports journalist PA Gullö, who hosts the podcast Camino med PA. We met at a café right next to the cathedral in León, and recorded an episode. Unfortunately, the audio didn’t turn out well, so we had to re-record it a bit later. It was great to be part of podcast Camino med PA part 12, and we even got the chance to mention our Website! We wrapped up the day with a delicious pasta dinner at a cozy restaurant on the plaza in front of the cathedral. A busy and different kind of Camino day with no walking, but full of people, projects, and new experiences. That too, is part of the journey.",
